{%- comment -%}
  Full-text index for the archive filter, built at deploy time.

  The header filter used to match `post.title` only, which on a 188-entry
  archive meant "docker" found nothing unless a title happened to contain
  the word. This ships title, tags and body so the field searches what the
  posts actually say.

  Keys are one letter because the array repeats them 188 times: `body`
  instead of `b` alone would add several KB of nothing but key names.
  Bodies are lowercased here rather than in the browser so the client does
  no per-keystroke case folding, and `strip_html` + `normalize_whitespace`
  drop the markup and the indentation runs that Jekyll leaves behind.

  Fetched once, lazily, on the first keystroke — never on page load.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
{%- assign body = post.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | downcase -%}
{"t":{{ post.title | jsonify }},"u":{{ post.url | jsonify }},"g":{{ post.tags | join: " " | jsonify }},"b":{{ body | jsonify }}}
{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
